  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-45" contextRef="c-1">Q4</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="f-46" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="f-47" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="f-48" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="f-49" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4) None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-50" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;CP23-535-000 - South Spearfish Project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On August 28, 2023, WBI Energy Transmission, Inc. (WBI Energy), pursuant to Sections 7(c) and 7(b) of the NGA and Part 157 of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission&#8217;s (FERC or Commission) regulations, filed an Abbreviated Application for a Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity and Abandonment Authority requesting authorization to construct, uprate, modify, operate, and abandon natural gas facilities in Lawrence County, South Dakota.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;The project consisted of: 1) relocating pressure regulation and overpressure equipment for the Deadwood-Central City Lateral; 2) uprating the Deadwood-Central City Lateral; 3) constructing the new South Spearfish Station; 4) abandoning by sale to Montana-Dakota Utilities Co. the 4-inch-diameter South Spearfish Lateral and certain equipment at the South Spearfish Town Border Station; and 5) abandoning by removal the remaining equipment at the South Spearfish Town Border Station. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On June 12, 2024, the Commission issued WBI Energy a Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity and Abandonment Authority and on August 6, 2024, authorized WBI Energy to proceed with project activities. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On June 11, 2025, the Commission granted WBI Energy&#8217;s request to place project facilities into service and proceed with abandonment activities. The facilities were placed into service on July 1, 2025, and the abandonment activities were completed as of July 8, 2025. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;CP25-75-000 - Minot Expansion Project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On February 13, 2025, WBI Energy, pursuant to Section 7 of the NGA and Section 157.210 of the Commission&#8217;s regulations, filed a prior notice request for authorization to replace, modify, uprate, and operate certain natural gas facilities in Morton County, North Dakota. The project included: (1) the uprate of approximately 6.9 miles of the Cabin Creek &#8211; Bismarck Mainline; (2) the replacement of approximately 2.3 miles of the 12-inch diameter Heskett Line with 16-inch diameter pipeline; (3) the replacement of approximately 0.5 mile of the 12-inch diameter Cabin Creek-Bismarck Mainline and Cabin Creek &#8211; Bismarck Loop Line with a single 12-inch diameter pipeline; (4) the relocation of the Sweet Briar Transfer Station to the Highway 25 Valve Setting; and (5) the modification and replacement of several aboveground facilities in conjunction with the uprate and pipeline replacements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On February 21, 2025, the Commission issued its &#8220;Notice of Request Under Blanket Authorization.&#8221; No protests to WBI Energy&#8217;s request were filed. Therefore, the proposed activity was authorized on April 23, 2025. Facilities associated with the project were placed into service November 1, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;CP25-166-000 - 2025 Baker Storage Well Abandonment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On March 31, 2025, WBI Energy, pursuant to Section 7 of the NGA and Section 157.216(b) of the Commission&#8217;s regulations, filed a prior notice request for the authorization to abandon six natural gas storage wells, approximately 4.07 miles of associated three-inch, four-inch, and twelve-inch diameter natural gas storage pipeline, and five aboveground measurement facilities, all located in WBI Energy&#8217;s Baker Storage Field in Fallon County, Montana. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;On April 10, 2025, the FERC issued its &#8220;Notice of Request Under Blanket Authorization and Establishing Intervention and Protest Deadline.&#8221; No protests to WBI Energy&#8217;s request were filed. Therefore, the proposed activity was authorized on June 10, 2025. The abandonment of the natural gas storage wells and certain pipeline facilities were completed by November 9, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-51" contextRef="c-1">WBI Energy Transmission, Inc.</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
