    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amounts allocated to WBI Energy Transmission are based upon the Modified Massachusetts Formula, the number of employees or other time tracking mechanisms. Other miscellaneous allocation methodologies are also utilized to some extent.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The amount includes charges for human resources, accounting, safety, executive and other administrative services.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Includes goods and/or services provided by MDU Resources Group, Inc., Montana-Dakota Utilities Co., and CEHI, LLC. These expenses have been allocated to the Company on the basis of direct usage when identifiable, with the remainder allocated on the basis of allocation percentages of a 3-factor formula, which includes gross plant, net revenues and labor, the percent of total average commercial paper borrowings at Centennial or other allocation methodologies that are considered to be a reasonable reflection of the utilization of the services provided to the benefits received.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This amount includes charges for legal, treasury services, risk management, auditing, tax, executive, director's fees, and other administrative services. It also includes charges for IT, human resources and payroll processing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The Landeck Compressor Station was not operated in 2025. The sale of the remaining unit at the station and all abandonment activities were completed by September 19, 2024.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The Spring Creek Compressor Station was not operated in 2025. The station is still operational and retirement is not contemplated.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Reflects weighted average BTU content of 1.01434 based on a total cushion gas capacity of 157,598,700 Mcf certificated in Docket Nos. CP82-487-014, CP82-487-034 and CP17-469-000. The basis for this BTU content is the weighted average of WBI Energy Transmission's storage fields using the estimated 1/1/96 BTU content at the Baker Storage field of 0.993 and Elk Basin Storage field of 1.042 for native cushion gas and 2025 BTU content at the Baker Storage field of 1.01826 and Elk Basin Storage field of 1.04891 for injected cushion gas.</span>
